                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "45e55810-272e-4d63-aa17-126d9fad1245",
                        "source_entry_id": "d1177fe3-b1e2-3b58-b5f4-e830b11776e6",
                        "source_sense_id": "ac14e334-94e3-35b3-83f9-7fc020b3dcc9",
                        "target_lang_word": "Mandarin orange",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Mandarin orange",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ea48d4b1-725e-3a65-93db-160e19283451",
                                        "entry_id": "6d063c44-25c6-384f-9ff2-971d3ed3606a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative letter-case form of mandarin orange."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80beb20a-7e24-4d6d-a1a7-a51bec8d2087",
                                                "sense_id": "ea48d4b1-725e-3a65-93db-160e19283451",
                                                "text": "A number of the Chinese varieties of oranges are in the garden, including the Citrus nobilis, or Mandarin orange, and numerous others."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d26c9a1-a63b-44d7-90bb-8a14bc5b7c2d",
                                                "sense_id": "ea48d4b1-725e-3a65-93db-160e19283451",
                                                "text": "Some of the very richest are only made in brown and black, and are meant for mantles as well as dresses, but there are three new dominant colours—Mandarin, a rich yellow like the rind of a Mandarin orange; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc742301-e58a-42ba-bf5f-6b9353cc7238",
                                                "sense_id": "ea48d4b1-725e-3a65-93db-160e19283451",
                                                "text": "After Earl died and I was alone again, I stopped cooking all those big dinners and lived on cottage cheese and canned Mandarin oranges for weeks."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c4c31e09-f569-4d1e-a555-5e1e43d2b98d",
                                                "sense_id": "ea48d4b1-725e-3a65-93db-160e19283451",
                                                "text": "Optional: ½ cup Mandarin orange segments"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b18a5127-b7f4-4040-87a9-9b4462c64ad5",
                                                "sense_id": "ea48d4b1-725e-3a65-93db-160e19283451",
                                                "text": "11-ounce can Mandarin orange segments, drained (optional)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "601e6186-30f3-4783-b165-a9e69424a7aa",
                                                "sense_id": "ea48d4b1-725e-3a65-93db-160e19283451",
                                                "text": "Stir together ½ c drained Mandarin orange segments in light syrup, 2 Tbsp orange marmalade, 1 Tbsp chopped scallions, 1 Tbsp low-fat red wine vinaigrette, and a pinch of ground allspice. […] Toss together 6 oz (1½ c) cubed deli (or leftover) turkey breast, 1 can (8.5 oz) drained Mandarin orange segments in light syrup, 3 Tbsp low-fat honey mustard dressing, 1 Tbsp orange marmalade, and 2 Tbsp chopped cashews."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e97b2f1d-ca22-444a-aa9c-76f94081d4cb",
                                                "sense_id": "ea48d4b1-725e-3a65-93db-160e19283451",
                                                "text": "Clementines, by the way, are in the Mandarin orange family, which also includes tangerines."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b87df57-34ef-4e46-be0a-96ebca844146",
                                                "sense_id": "ea48d4b1-725e-3a65-93db-160e19283451",
                                                "text": "Flipping through the “Salad” section I found the ’80s represented with a recipe for honey mustard poppyseed dressing. Why don’t I make that any more? I loved it at the time over a bed of romaine, cilantro, Mandarin oranges, avocados and tomatoes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1827f283-e8f0-4e99-9581-e3e496344c4b",
                                                "sense_id": "ea48d4b1-725e-3a65-93db-160e19283451",
                                                "text": "8-oz can Mandarin orange segments, drained, optional"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf9d6a0b-e8ca-47a8-bd84-9ca16f2fa188",
                                                "sense_id": "ea48d4b1-725e-3a65-93db-160e19283451",
                                                "text": "Clementines, a variety of Mandarin orange, are plentiful in winter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77729eca-f9b4-4c47-b023-834fea50b7ae",
                                                "sense_id": "ea48d4b1-725e-3a65-93db-160e19283451",
                                                "text": "Citrus fruits (Citrus hybrids), including kumquat, Mandarin orange, satsuma and ‘Meyer’ lemon, are among the easiest fruit trees to grow organically in Zones 8b to 10."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4fdd1339-b95d-4749-8f17-46238b62df44",
                                                "sense_id": "ea48d4b1-725e-3a65-93db-160e19283451",
                                                "text": "3–4 Mandarin oranges, peeled and sliced, or pomegranate seeds, for serving"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8711216a-c601-416f-aeaf-a91a4440ddb2",
                        "source_entry_id": "d1177fe3-b1e2-3b58-b5f4-e830b11776e6",
                        "source_sense_id": "ac14e334-94e3-35b3-83f9-7fc020b3dcc9",
                        "target_lang_word": "mandarin",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mandarin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1abfeb3f-b579-346c-8fb7-000f6d7bd8a3",
                                        "entry_id": "04b20cc0-92a7-3bfa-b4a4-ebe488b6fea9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A high government bureaucrat of the Chinese Empire."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38f3383c-7829-4ae8-97f8-8279e26dc5e4",
                                                "sense_id": "1abfeb3f-b579-346c-8fb7-000f6d7bd8a3",
                                                "text": "LIKE THE MANDARINS of old, the rulers of China live behind high walls. When they emerge, which they rarely do, they travel in cars with rear windows curtained like sedan chairs.\nThey live in the Chung Nan Hai, a walled park adjacent to the Forbidden City from where ancient dynasties ruled the Celestial Empire."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c2e8c865-967a-3fca-bd06-eb55cdb9002f",
                                        "entry_id": "04b20cc0-92a7-3bfa-b4a4-ebe488b6fea9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A pedantic or elitist bureaucrat."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c0cb748d-3844-3b4b-ae4f-ce66f29f4a8d",
                                        "entry_id": "04b20cc0-92a7-3bfa-b4a4-ebe488b6fea9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A pedantic senior person of influence in academia or literary circles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "sometimes"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ddf0fce2-e76a-47a6-9a39-90d7bbd361ff",
                                                "sense_id": "c0cb748d-3844-3b4b-ae4f-ce66f29f4a8d",
                                                "text": "Its sting preserved to literature a fierce peculiar genius [Waugh] who, in the 40 years before his death last week at 62, achieved recognition as the grand old mandarin of modern British prose and as a satirist whose skill at sticking pens in people rates him a roomy cell in the murderers’ row (Swift, Pope, Wilde, Shaw) of English letters."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e984fd2-79de-4b9c-b589-3d2bc5e0cf92",
                                                "sense_id": "c0cb748d-3844-3b4b-ae4f-ce66f29f4a8d",
                                                "text": "When mandarins on the court pointed to obscure language in the Constitution to overturn a century of precedent and declare the income tax unconstitutional, Harlan sided with precedent[.]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cdafb1ea-4305-443c-b980-ae02d13765d3",
                                                "sense_id": "c0cb748d-3844-3b4b-ae4f-ce66f29f4a8d",
                                                "text": "When institutional mandarins such as this eminent pair set out to undermine the traditional basis for remunerating the products of the mind, you might expect a lowly scribe (such as your reviewer) to take umbrage."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e4888d03-b356-3a31-9e36-9a8c0929112e",
                                        "entry_id": "04b20cc0-92a7-3bfa-b4a4-ebe488b6fea9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ellipsis of mandarin duck."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "ellipsis"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3a7ff01e-a055-3fc1-bd88-f160c90e2f5c",
                                        "entry_id": "04b20cc0-92a7-3bfa-b4a4-ebe488b6fea9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A senior civil servant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd9a25dd-b11c-3283-83a5-f847efa7253e",
                                        "entry_id": "04b20cc0-92a7-3bfa-b4a4-ebe488b6fea9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A figurine of a Chinese person with movable head that was popular in the 1950s. (Cf. bobblehead.)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b4c576a0-9296-478b-8e85-a9cdc5d37572",
                                                "sense_id": "fd9a25dd-b11c-3283-83a5-f847efa7253e",
                                                "text": "He lay quietly in the hydropathic bed while his heart shuddered and his eyes focused at random on objects in the room, simulating a calm he could not feel. The walls of green jade, the nightlight in the porcelain mandarin whose head nodded interminably if you touched him, the multi-clock that radiated the time of three planets and six satelittes, the bed itself, a crystal pool flowing with carbonated glycerine at ninety-nine point nine Fahrenheit."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "mandarin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "55a6f6a7-ef6b-319f-a73c-6f11585dbdfe",
                                        "entry_id": "0d15f147-dee7-3324-9d78-d9222e691da0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pertaining to or reminiscent of mandarins; deliberately superior or complex; esoteric, highbrow, obscurantist."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e8bd867-3057-40ac-8f32-9588d1861939",
                                                "sense_id": "55a6f6a7-ef6b-319f-a73c-6f11585dbdfe",
                                                "text": "A mandarin impassivity had descended over Smiley's face. The earlier emotion was quite gone."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "13ce901b-ddeb-4271-aa93-41120defa0dc",
                                                "sense_id": "55a6f6a7-ef6b-319f-a73c-6f11585dbdfe",
                                                "text": "[Anatole] Broyard's columns were suffused with both worldliness and high culture. Wry, mandarin, even self-amused at times, he wrote like a man about town, but one who just happened to have all of Western literature at his fingertips."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b54b34e-18f5-461a-aa80-c564fc27be2d",
                                                "sense_id": "55a6f6a7-ef6b-319f-a73c-6f11585dbdfe",
                                                "text": "Though alert to riddles' strong roots in vernacular narrative, Cook's tastes are mandarin, and she gives a loving account of Wallace Stevens's meditations on the life of poetic images and simile […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
